.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-accounts - Every account: find one, read it, switch it off or on (lists when run bare)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin accounts [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List every account, as the operator reads them: the whole record, with the operator's
switch (active, status) and whether the account holds the operator grant (admin).

.PP
--search finds an account from whatever is at hand: a part of its name or of its email,
a wallet address or its beginning (0x…), or its id.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for accounts

.PP
\fB--operator\fP=""
	Only accounts that hold the operator grant ('true') or that do not ('false')

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--search\fP=""
	A part of the name or email, a wallet address or its beginning (0x…), or the account's id

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort by name, email or created_at (prefix - for descending; default: name)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=""
	Only accounts with this status: active or deactivated


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin accounts
  rail0 admin accounts --search acme --pretty
  rail0 admin accounts --search 0x2D2B…            # whose wallet is this
  rail0 admin accounts --status deactivated
  rail0 admin accounts --operator true             # who holds the operator grant
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-accounts-activate(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-accounts-deactivate(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-accounts-exposure(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-accounts-get(1)\fP
